Ladybird stops margins collapsing through a box only where placing the
box introduced clearance, not wherever its clear isn’t none. Blink does
the same: Its ApplyClearance() moves a box, and reports clearance, only
where the box would otherwise sit above the clearance offset of the
floats it clears. Gecko’s nsBlockFrame::ReflowBlockFrame() likewise
treats a block with clearance only when it has floats to clear.
